1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,133
I'm moving my game
from Three.js to Godot.

2
00:00:04,133 --> 00:00:07,000
Does that mean starting over?

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,067
For the code, yes. For
the whole project? No.

4
00:00:11,067 --> 00:00:15,467
Heartwoodfall started
as a Three.js project.

5
00:00:15,467 --> 00:00:19,000
Claude helped me fix the
character movement.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,933
Now I'm rebuilding in Godot.

7
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:27,300
The original still guides the characters,
environments, and interface.

8
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:32,233
Some assets may carry over,
including my 3D models.

9
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:36,033
A new engine means
rebuilding the foundation,

10
00:00:36,033 --> 00:00:39,867
not throwing away every useful idea.

11
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:44,633
Follow my Heartwoodfall
devlog for the next build.
